# Angular Development Patterns

## 🧱 Component Architecture

### Component Structure Convention
All components follow this standard structure:

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-component-name',
  templateUrl: './component-name.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./component-name.component.css']
})
export class ComponentNameComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {
  // Public properties first
  public property: type;
  
  // Private properties
  private destroySubject: Subject<void> = new Subject();
  
  constructor(private service: ServiceName) {}
  
  ngOnInit() {
    // Initialization logic with proper subscription management
    this.service.data$
      .pipe(takeUntil(this.destroySubject))
      .subscribe(data => {
        // Handle data
      });
  }
  
  ngOnDestroy() {
    this.destroySubject.next();
    this.destroySubject.unsubscribe();
  }
}
```

### Key Patterns Used in Fledge GUI

#### 1. Module-Based Architecture
- Feature modules for logical grouping ([DashboardModule](mdc:src/app/components/core/dashboard/dashboard.module.ts))
- Shared modules for common functionality ([SharedModule](mdc:src/app/shared.module.ts))

#### 2. Subscription Management
Always use the destroy pattern to prevent memory leaks:
```typescript
private destroySubject: Subject<void> = new Subject();

// In ngOnInit
.pipe(takeUntil(this.destroySubject))

// In ngOnDestroy
this.destroySubject.next();
this.destroySubject.unsubscribe();
```

#### 3. Service Injection Patterns
Use proper dependency injection with typed services:
```typescript
constructor(
  private alertService: AlertService,
  private sharedService: SharedService,
  private router: Router
) {}
```

## 🔄 State Management Patterns

### BehaviorSubject Usage
Services use BehaviorSubjects for reactive state management:

```typescript
@Injectable()
export class ServiceName {
  public dataSubject: BehaviorSubject<DataType> = new BehaviorSubject<DataType>(initialValue);
  
  public get data$() {
    return this.dataSubject.asObservable();
  }
}
```

### Shared Service Pattern
The [SharedService](mdc:src/app/services/shared.service.ts) manages global application state:
- User authentication state
- Theme preferences
- Sidebar collapse state
- Connection status

## 🛡️ Route Guards & Security

### Guard Implementation
Route guards protect sensitive areas:
- `AuthRequiredGuard`: Requires valid authentication token
- `DataViewRoleGuard`: Restricts access based on user roles
- `AdminGuard`: Admin-only route protection

### Usage in Routing
```typescript
{
  path: 'admin-area',
  component: AdminComponent,
  canActivate: [AuthRequiredGuard, AdminGuard]
}
```

## 🎨 Template Patterns

### Reactive Forms
Use reactive forms for complex form handling:
```typescript
this.form = this.formBuilder.group({
  field: ['', [Validators.required, Validators.email]]
});
```

### Async Pipe Usage
Prefer async pipe over manual subscriptions:
```html
<div *ngIf="service.data$ | async as data">
  {{ data.property }}
</div>
```

### Conditional Rendering
Use proper Angular conditional directives:
```html
<div *ngIf="isVisible; else loadingTemplate">
  Content
</div>
<ng-template #loadingTemplate>
  Loading...
</ng-template>
```

## 🔧 Lifecycle Hooks

### OnInit Pattern
Initialize component data and subscriptions:
```typescript
async ngOnInit() {
  // Async initialization if needed
  await this.loadInitialData();
  
  // Set up subscriptions
  this.setupSubscriptions();
}
```

### OnDestroy Pattern
Always implement OnDestroy for cleanup:
```typescript
ngOnDestroy() {
  this.destroySubject.next();
  this.destroySubject.unsubscribe();
}
```

## 📡 HTTP & API Patterns

### Service Methods
API services should return observables:
```typescript
getData(): Observable<DataType> {
  return this.http.get<DataType>(`${this.apiUrl}/data`);
}
```

### Error Handling
Implement proper error handling:
```typescript
this.service.getData()
  .pipe(
    catchError(error => {
      this.alertService.error(error.message);
      return of(null);
    })
  )
  .subscribe(data => {
    // Handle successful response
  });
```

## 🎯 Performance Optimization

### Change Detection
Use OnPush strategy where appropriate for better performance.

### Lazy Loading
Implement lazy loading for feature modules to reduce initial bundle size.

### TrackBy Functions
Use trackBy functions with *ngFor for better list performance:
```html
<div *ngFor="let item of items; trackBy: trackByFn">
  {{ item.name }}
</div>
```